const BOM: [u8; 3] = [0xEF, 0xBB, 0xBF];

/// The status of UTF-8 BOM detection at the start of a stream.
///
/// A BOM is only recognized when it is the first thing in a stream, so this
/// detector is active only for a fresh reader (or after a call to `reset`).
/// The BOM may arrive split across multiple caller-provided buffers, so the
/// detector remembers any unmatched prefix. Once the BOM is either confirmed
/// or ruled out, detection is permanently disabled for the remainder of the
/// stream (unless the parser is reset).
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
enum BomState {
    /// The BOM has not been confirmed or ruled out yet. `bom_len` records how
    /// many leading BOM bytes (`0`, `1` or `2`) have been observed.
    Checking,
    /// The BOM was found and removed. No further BOM detection is done.
    Found,
    /// The BOM was ruled out (or no detection is required). Any held prefix
    /// bytes are replayed to the parser through `bom_pos`.
    None,
}

